## 2. Red-Proof Sabotage 1 — computeLineHash
Asserted condition: `bun test` must fail when line hashes are wrong; `hashEditFile`
fail-closed anchor validation depends on `computeLineHash` (FNV-1a 4-hex).
Sabotage (transient, via native edit tool on src/editors/hashline-tools.ts):
  OLD:
    export function computeLineHash(line: string): string {
      const text = line.trim();
      let hash = 0x811c9dc5;
      for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {
        hash ^= text.charCodeAt(i);
        hash = Math.imul(hash, 0x01000193);
      }
      const narrowed = (hash >>> 0) & 0xffff;
      return narrowed.toString(16).padStart(4, "0");
    }
  NEW:
    export function computeLineHash(line: string): string {
      void line;
      return "0000";
    }
$ bun test
  (fail) computeLineHash > empty and whitespace-only lines hash the FNV offset basis low 16 bits
    Expected: "9dc5"  Received: "0000"  (test/editors.test.ts:55)
  (fail) computeLineHash > distinct lines usually hash distinctly
    Expected: 5  Received: 1  (test/editors.test.ts:63)
  (fail) hashEditFile > fails closed when the anchor drifted beyond the 25-line window
    Expected: false  Received: true  (test/editors.test.ts:228)
  59 pass, 3 fail, 215 expect() calls
